Z||000000||BAM-BAM||06-18-2001||12:09 AM|||| Scenario; My oldest son broke my door key in my lock.<P> Solution; bought new doorlocks from Fiero Store.<P> Problem; Dropped retainer clip between door skin and door frame.<P> Question; How the H$LL do I remove the door skin?<BR>  <BR> Thanks; for ever inbebted to anyone who can give me a step by step to remove the outer door skin from my 885GT with aero moulding.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||9
Z||000001||cadaver||06-18-2001||01:33 AM||||Thats an easy one. Get a magnet on a stick. You know those antenna ones. AND DONT REMOVE THE DOOR SKIN TO DO LOCKS. There are fasteners you will destroy when you remove them and will have to find replacements. <BR>I just did locks in mine about two weeks ago. It took an hour for both sides.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||06-18-2001||01:34 AM||||Make the KID do it!!!!!<P>hehe just kidding....<P>Remove inner door panel<P>Remove outside mirror<P>remove 4 or 5 Rivits from underside of outside door panel.<P>Remove Torks screws at fwd and rear edges of door panel.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||06-18-2001||02:08 AM||||  Thanks guys, that's great. Archie, thanks for the steps. If I don't have to remove the door skin I don't want to. Tom, can you give me some details? I got the old lock out ok and the new one in place, it's the retainer clip that is giving me a hard time. The big one behind the lock plate and infront of the outer skin, the oversized C clip. Any secrets? LMK<P>Peace, Don<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||fierofrek||06-18-2001||04:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Make the KID do it!!!!!<P>hehe just kidding....<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>ROTFLMAO!!!!!!!!!<P>I remember once when I was 16, I borrowed dads car, and locked the ignition key inside the car and dad refused to come help me out with the spare. the weekend before we replaced the lock on the trunk, so I had the trunk key with me and ended up having to crawl through the little space in the back of the seat. LOL, to say the least it taught me to never lock the keys in the car! (knocks on wood)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000005||skitime||06-18-2001||07:54 AM||||Maybe I am missing something here but how would you replace the door lock without removing the door panel anyway?<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||06-18-2001||08:11 AM||||  Not the door pannel, the door skin, on the out side. just a matter of accessability.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000007||theogre||06-18-2001||07:54 PM||||Well, I'm looking at a door skin.... I guess you might be able to work the big clip of the cylinder with very long needle nose pliers. Looks like a real ____ with the door on.<P>The small clip that holds the rod has a trick to it.<P>The clip has to be removed to release the rod.<P>the trick... put the clip back in place on the new lock before you install it. After the lock is installed in the skin, shove the rod in the hole. The rod will snap into the clip easily.||||reg||1
Z||000008||BAM-BAM||06-18-2001||10:49 PM||||  Thanks Ogre, but Cadaver said it can be done from the inside without removing the door skin. That is what I want to know how to do. I droped that big "C" clip between the door frame and the skin. I haven't yet tried to fish it out. I'm waiting to hear from Tom.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000009||tgowens||06-19-2001||01:14 AM||||Bam-Bam, I have done it through the top of the door (remove the rubber piece at the rear of the dew strips) with a long flat blade screwdriver. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||cadaver||06-19-2001||02:49 AM||||Waiting on lil ole me. Awww schucks.<BR>This is what I did. after you retrieve the clip with a magnet. Remove the outer rub strip or what ever you call that black molding the runs along the door. You dont need to remove the whole thing just like the three aft clips. There is also a plastic pin at the door handle. Once this is loose you can get to the screw that is just in front of the door handle. It goes to a black plastic stand off. Remove the screw 7mm the remove the standoff from inside . Slide it forward. Then you can get the clip in with little trouble. You will need some long needle nose vise grips or similar. The problem I had was the clip was very tight on the new lock body. I just got it started the put a piece of wood I think it was an old broom handle on the back of the clip through a panel opening and tapped it with a hammer. If you need any more help just let me know.<P>If this is no bueno you can loosen the door skin from the back and top without taking out the lower rivets. Then swing the plate that the lock attatches to out the rear of the opening and work it there.||||reg||1
Z||000011||BAM-BAM||06-19-2001||07:51 AM||||  Thanks Tom. That's what I have been waiting for. That and a new steering column. Anywho, I'll give the old Ivy League heav ho, and get back with you when I need, if I need more assistance.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
